{
  "name": "A Bengali primer's own tables, transcribed",
  "WHY_THIS_FILE_EXISTS": [
    "Everything here comes from pages of a Bangladeshi primer, supplied as images. It is a better",
    "source than anything this repository could assemble: the words were chosen by someone who",
    "teaches children to read, which is exactly what tools/kar-words.json had to approximate by",
    "mining a frequency corpus and then throwing most of it away.",
    "",
    "Four tables the primer has that the game did not:",
    "",
    "  no_kar   Word building from bare letters - ব + ক = বক. The game teaches aksharas, so a",
    "           word with no কার at all is the simplest case and had no page of its own.",
    "  by_kar   A word list per কার, where the বারোখড়ি could show one mined example.",
    "  phala    The six ফলা, plus রেফ - the shrunk forms a consonant takes inside a conjunct.",
    "           Each carries the forms the primer prints and the words it gives for them.",
    "  jukto    যুক্তবর্ণ: 103 conjuncts, each with its parts and its words. This is the table",
    "           that explains the game's own rule - ক্ষ is one letter, so it is one tile.",
    "",
    "Transcribed by hand from photographs, which is a source that goes wrong silently, so none of",
    "it is trusted. `primer()` in tools/build.py re-derives every claim on every build: each",
    "equation is split and compared against its own parts, each word is confirmed to carry the কার",
    "it is filed under, each যুক্তবর্ণ's parts are hasanta-joined and compared to the letter they",
    "are said to make, and each form is confirmed to be a single akshara by the same splitter the",
    "board uses. A failure raises. Every word was also checked against wordfreq's 120,000 attested",
    "Bengali words.",
    "",
    "`spelling_notes` records what was left out and why - words the primer spells in a way modern",
    "Bangladeshi standard does not (গগণ, কলসী, দূর্বা), proper nouns (আলী, গীতা, মিনি), rows where",
    "the printed table put a word under the wrong mark (ভস্ম under ষ্ম, when it carries স্ম), and",
    "words no corpus attests. Left out rather than corrected: a table a child reads to learn",
    "spelling must not contain a misspelling, and it is not this repository's place to silently",
    "rewrite a teacher's book either - so the reason is written down instead.",
    "",
    "`unused`, on each ফলা, lists the forms the primer prints that no attested Bengali word uses -",
    "খ্ব, ঙ্ম, ঠ্র and 16 others. The alphabet allows them; the language does not use them. Shown",
    "dimmed on the page rather than dropped, because the full set of shapes is the lesson."
  ],
